  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2024 Workplace First Aid Zambia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NLRC has provided structured investment (including a contribution to the running costs) and technical support for ZRCS&#x2019; workplace first aid business from 2017-2021. In 2022 ZRCS took on 100% of the running costs of the business, whilst NLRC still provided technical support where needed and supported specific investments into the business as outlined below. The level of business growth during that 5 year period has exceeded expectations, which has enabled ZRCS to take more control of their financial situation, to resolve debts, facilitate NS investment and development, and fulfil more of their humanitarian ambition. Market knowledge indicates that there is further growth to be found &#x2013; many companies and organisations do not purchase first aid training, other competitors are growing in different markets, existing customers are requesting additional training products from ZRCS, and the government is very keen to develop a training system for new drivers. In 2022 NLRC provided funding to allow the WFA business to innovate and take risks &#x2013; with support for a professional level advertising campaign. The WFA business has experienced consistent growth since its inception in 2016, except during the Covid-19 disruption in 2020. Growth is measured in both revenue and surplus. From 2016 to 2023, the compound annual growth rate for revenue was 25%. In 2023, the profit margin reached 37%, and the business generated approximately 70,000 Euros in unrestricted funding for ZRCS. The first five months of 2024 have seen revenue maintain at the 2023 level, with expectations for further growth</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The 20k investment will be used to engage a Marketing Consultancy firm to develop among others a Regional Marketing campaigns outside Lusaka. Besides, ZRCS will start to make use of a Brand Ambassador-Social Media Influencer.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To support the further growth of the WFA business, and therefore the financial sustainability of the ZRCS</narrative>
  </description>
